        "CustomSupportsReborn": {
            "filename": "/home/daniel/.cache/cura/5.10/cura_packages/CustomSupportsReborn.curapackage",
            "package_info": {
                "author": {
                    "author_id": "SlasheeTheCow",
                    "display_name": "Slashee the Cow",
                    "email": "slasheethecow@gmail.com",
                    "website": "https://github.com/slashee-the-cow"
                },
                "description": "Create custom supports of several different shapes (or my favourite, click two points on your model and it'll do a line of support between them) to hold things up the way YOU want them. Don't let the automatic supports force you to do things their way any more.\n\nSupports can taper outwards (little top, big bottom) to hold up little bits of model without support so small it'll fall over. Set the taper angle to a negative value and they'll go inwards! Big top, small bottom, perfect for when you're running low on filament... or when you want to make sure you don't run low on filament :)\n\nThis is based on the Custom Support Cylinder plugin by 5axes, but I've updated it to make sure it works with current versions of Cura and added a few new features.\n\nGot any problems? Suggestions? Want to say hi? Come by the site and I'll be happy to see you!",
                "display_name": "Custom Supports Reborn",
                "is_active": true,
                "is_bundled": false,
                "is_installed": true,
                "package_id": "CustomSupportsReborn",
                "package_type": "plugin",
                "package_version": "1.2.0",
                "sdk_version": 8,
                "sdk_version_semver": "8.9.0",
                "website": "https://github.com/Slashee-the-Cow/CustomSupportsReborn"
            }
        },
        "DirectSupportBlockersReborn": {
            "filename": "/home/daniel/.cache/cura/5.12/cura_packages/DirectSupportBlockersReborn.curapackage",
            "package_info": {
                "author": {
                    "author_id": "SlasheeTheCow",
                    "display_name": "Slashee the Cow",
                    "email": "slasheethecow@gmail.com",
                    "website": "https://github.com/slashee-the-cow"
                },
                "description": "Don't start with a tiny cube! Infinite shapes to make support blockers out of!\n\nBox\nSet the width, depth and height and click your object to create one, then move it where it's needed.  \n\nCylinder\nJust pick your diameter and height, click your object, and move it into position!\n\nSquare/Rectangular Pyramid\nDefine sizes for the top and bottom (it can go from small to big or vice versa) and height.\n- Normal supports will only avoid the part which intersects your model.\n- Tree supports will avoid the whole pyramid.\n\nLine\nClick two points on your model and it will draw a line of support blocker between them.\n\nCustom\nTurn any model into a support blocker! Works super if you need thing really specific. (Which is sort of the point.)\nRemember to move your custom blocker to intersect with the surface of the model that needs blocking.\n\nAll built in types can be a fixed height or go down to the build plate.\n\nInspired as a follow-up to \"Custom Support Eraser Plus\" by 5@xes but not based on it.",
                "display_name": "Direct Support Blockers Reborn",
                "is_active": true,
                "is_bundled": false,
                "is_installed": true,
                "package_id": "DirectSupportBlockersReborn",
                "package_type": "plugin",
                "package_version": "1.0.2",
                "sdk_version": 8,
                "sdk_version_semver": "8.10.0",
                "website": "https://github.com/Slashee-the-Cow/DirectSupportBlockersReborn"
            }
        },
