                "description": "Sick of warping but don't want to put 20 lines of brim all around something? Get something more targeted! This lets you - or the automatic function :) - put round \"tabs\" on the corners of objects to hold them securely in place.\n\nThe tabs are printed as support so they're quite easy to remove, especially the \"dish\" shaped ones, which are also easier to get off the build plate. You can specify the diameter and height of the tabs. After creation, tabs can be individually moved or deleted as required.\n\nOriginally created by 5@xes. For the Reborn version, I've updated and optimised all the code, made sure it works on current versions of Cura and threw in a couple of small new features which seemed like they'd be useful.",
